From: h96 work order 2026-09-14
Subject: [PATCH] ASoC: meson: aiu: default the HDMI source mux to I2S

Measured on the box with audio playing: pcm0p is RUNNING, S16_LE stereo 48 kHz, the hardware
pointer advances and there is not a single XRUN - yet every widget from the I2S FIFO to HDMITX TX
is Off, so nothing reaches the sink.

    AIU I2S FIFO Playback      Off  in 1 out 0
    AIU I2S Encoder Playback   Off  in 1 out 0
    AIU HDMI I2S IN Playback   Off  in 1 out 0     <- no output
    AIU HDMI CTRL SRC          Off  in 0 out 1     <- no input
    HDMITX I2S Playback / TX   Off

The chain is broken at exactly one point, the "AIU HDMI CTRL SRC" mux. Its enum reads
CTRL_DATA_SEL of AIU_HDMI_CLK_DATA_CTRL, which is zero after reset - "DISABLED" - and nothing
sets it. This image carries neither tinymix nor alsa_ctl, and the AIDL audio HAL does not apply
mixer path files, so the control is never touched.

Setting it to I2S from userspace powered the whole chain in one step, which is what establishes
the diagnosis rather than inferring it:

    AIU I2S Encoder Playback   Off -> On       AIU HDMI CTRL SRC     Off -> On
    AIU I2S FIFO Playback      Off -> On       AIU HDMI OUT Capture  Off -> On
    AIU HDMI I2S IN Playback   Off -> On       HDMITX I2S Playback   Off -> On
    be.dai-link-4-playback     Off -> On       HDMITX TX             Off -> On

That setting is lost on the next boot, which also explains the owner's report that HDMI sound
used to work and then stopped.

Initialise the field at component probe, writing the same two fields and the same value that the
mux's own put handler writes for I2S. Userspace can still change the control afterwards; this
replaces the reset default only.

Scope, stated plainly: this changes the default for every board using this driver, not only this
one. It is correct for a board whose sole audio output is HDMI, which is the case here; a board
wired to the analogue codec still selects ACODEC at runtime as before.

Audibility itself is not claimed here - the DAPM graph and the PCM state are what was measured.

--- a/sound/soc/meson/aiu-codec-ctrl.c
+++ b/sound/soc/meson/aiu-codec-ctrl.c
@@ -20,6 +20,9 @@
 	"DISABLED", "PCM", "I2S",
 };
 
+/* h96 0029: indeks "I2S" v aiu_codec_ctrl_mux_texts - on zhe znachenie polya */
+#define AIU_HDMI_CTRL_SRC_I2S	2
+
 static int aiu_codec_ctrl_mux_put_enum(struct snd_kcontrol *kcontrol,
 				       struct snd_ctl_elem_value *ucontrol)
 {
@@ -129,8 +132,34 @@
 	return aiu_of_xlate_dai_name(component, args, dai_name, AIU_HDMI);
 }
 
+/*
+ * h96 0029 (14.09.2026): vybrat' I2S kak istochnik HDMI-zvuka po umolchaniyu.
+ *
+ * Posle sbrosa pole CTRL_DATA_SEL registra AIU_HDMI_CLK_DATA_CTRL ravno nulyu,
+ * to est' mux stoit v "DISABLED", i ves' put' ot AIU I2S FIFO do HDMITX TX
+ * ostaetsya obestochennym: PCM igraet, ukazatel' idet, a zvuka net. Vystavlyat'
+ * etot kontrol nekomu - v obraze net ni tinymix, ni alsa_ctl, a shtatnyj AIDL-HAL
+ * fajly mikshera ne primenyaet.
+ *
+ * Pishem te zhe dva polya i to zhe znachenie, chto i sobstvennyj .put muxa dlya
+ * I2S. Userspace po-prezhnemu mozhet pereklyuchit' kontrol - my tol'ko menyaem
+ * znachenie po umolchaniyu, a ne zapreshchaem vybor.
+ */
+static int aiu_hdmi_ctrl_component_probe(struct snd_soc_component *component)
+{
+	unsigned int i2s = AIU_HDMI_CTRL_SRC_I2S;
+
+	snd_soc_component_update_bits(component, AIU_HDMI_CLK_DATA_CTRL,
+				      CTRL_CLK_SEL | CTRL_DATA_SEL,
+				      FIELD_PREP(CTRL_CLK_SEL, i2s) |
+				      FIELD_PREP(CTRL_DATA_SEL, i2s));
+
+	return 0;
+}
+
 static const struct snd_soc_component_driver aiu_hdmi_ctrl_component = {
 	.name			= "AIU HDMI Codec Control",
+	.probe			= aiu_hdmi_ctrl_component_probe,
 	.dapm_widgets		= aiu_hdmi_ctrl_widgets,
 	.num_dapm_widgets	= ARRAY_SIZE(aiu_hdmi_ctrl_widgets),
 	.dapm_routes		= aiu_hdmi_ctrl_routes,
